WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.000
The inventory scan is cheap, because it
reads answers agencies have already given.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.088
It's useful only if every answer it questions
ends with an owner who goes and looks.

3
00:00:10.088 --> 00:00:15.381
Run over the published 2025 file, the
simple checks hit 72 percent of the live

4
00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:20.926
entries: more than half give no authorization
answer, and a third name no contact.

5
00:00:20.926 --> 00:00:24.813
Those are answers to reconcile,
not verdicts on agencies.

6
00:00:24.813 --> 00:00:29.004
The checks that matter most, like
an agent with no identity record,

7
00:00:29.004 --> 00:00:32.187
need the directory, so only
the agency can run them.

8
00:00:32.187 --> 00:00:36.994
The decision: run the checks on your own
submission every vintage, agentic and

9
00:00:36.994 --> 00:00:38.947
authorization findings first,

10
00:00:38.947 --> 00:00:42.401
and close a finding only when
a later look shows it fixed.

11
00:00:42.401 --> 00:00:43.490
And centrally?
